 Planets of the solar system in order: names, descriptions and interesting facts

The solar system is a group of planets orbiting in certain orbits around a bright star, which is called the Sun. This celestial body, together with all the satellites, was formed, according to scientists, as a result of the explosion of a supernova about 4.25 billion years ago. The solar system got its name a few decades later, when it was discovered that not only our planet, but all its satellites revolve around a star.

The inner planets of the solar system

According to the position of the Earth in the system, scientists have divided all planets into two groups. In one of them, the inner planets of the solar system were named, in the other - the outer ones. The first group includes:

Mercury;

Venus;

Earth;

Mars.

The inner planets of the solar system are also called terrestrial planets. They are smaller in size than other planets. Also, they are characterized by the presence of a solid surface.

